    "durationMs": 102155,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. The URL shortener is built with Express 4.21.2 (pinned) and `pg`, with all requirements tested end-to-end:\n\n**What I built**\n- `server.js` — all endpoints: `POST /links` (201 with generated or custom code, 409 duplicates, 422 for malformed JSON / invalid url / invalid code), `GET /links` (ascending order with `total`), `GET /links/:code` (404 unknown), `GET /r/:code` (302 + Location, increments clicks exactly once)\n- `migrate.js` + `migrations/001_create_links.sql` — pending-migration runner tracked in a `schema_migrations` table\n- `start.sh` — applies migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `README.md` — startup instructions\n\n**Verification results**\n- URL validation via WHATWG `URL`: requires absolute `http`/`https` with a host; submitted URL stored and returned byte-for-byte unchanged\n- Code validation: 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` enforced at both boundaries (4 and 20 pass, 3 and 21 fail)\n- Persistence confirmed across three server restarts (click counts carried over intact); migration re-runs are no-ops\n- Body parsing is content-type tolerant, so malformed JSON returns 422 regardless of headers\n- Fixed a subtle bug during testing: pg returns BIGINT as strings, so `clicks` is converted to a JSON number everywhere\n\nTest data was truncated and the test server stopped — the database is clean for the automated suite."
  }
